# Effective ignore list for the Semgrep SAST tiers.
#
# A committed .semgrepignore REPLACES Semgrep's built-in list wholesale, which
# is the reason to commit one: the built-in list silently drops test/, tests/,
# build/, dist/ and vendor/, and python/tests/ here starts a real ArangoDB and
# talks to it with real credentials, so it is exactly the tree that has to stay
# in scope. Every entry below is either a dependency directory, a VCS
# directory, generated build output, or the one dated exception at the bottom.
#
# THIS FILE IS GUARDED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, deliberately, because narrowing a
# SAST scope is how a SAST gate dies without ever going red:
#   * semgrep-scan/scan is passed semgrepignore-baseline: "src/ python/
#     python/tests/" (paths that must NOT be excluded) and fails if an entry
#     here would skip one of them.
#   * trivy-scan/disposition-check is passed the opposite-polarity parameter of
#     the same name, the allowlist of lines this file may contain, and fails on
#     any entry beyond it.
# Adding a line here therefore takes a reviewed change to
# semgrepignore-allowed in .circleci/config.yml as well.

.git/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
build/
dist/
target/
vendor/

# The committed test-server private key for the local ArangoDB fixture. It is
# a genuine finding (generic.secrets detected-private-key, ERROR) and it is
# excluded HERE, from SAST only, rather than being suppressed everywhere:
# the secret-scan tier still reports it every run, which is the tier whose job
# committed key material is. Excluding it from SAST keeps a single tracked
# finding from red-lining a gate that exists to catch first-party code defects.
# The real fix is to generate this key at fixture start-up instead of
# committing it; see Known gaps in SECURITY.md.
docker/server.pem
